The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ S A ], the reply is a fence containing S and A. The last object inside a code fence is A, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. For the rewritten text fence[ S ], the fence contains only S, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of S. Since A and S are different objects, the output changes, so the answer moves.